# =============================================================================
# DockAnalyzer — Analysis orchestration
# Section 1 — Header, imports, aliases and public interface
# =============================================================================

"""Central analysis orchestration for DockAnalyzer.

This module coordinates receptor and pose discovery, interaction analysis,
result consolidation, scoring, multipose comparison, reporting, export and
visualization. It provides the high-level execution layer that connects the
specialized DockAnalyzer modules without reimplementing their chemistry,
geometry, scoring, rendering or serialization logic.

The orchestration core is designed to support:

1. a single receptor-ligand pose;
2. multiple poses associated with the same receptor;
3. independent batch analysis requests;
4. ordinary Python objects and mapping-based synthetic inputs;
5. native UCSF ChimeraX sessions and molecular objects;
6. strict, permissive and partial-result execution policies.

Specialized modules are loaded only when required. This reduces circular
imports, preserves operation outside ChimeraX and allows later capability
inspection to report unavailable optional components accurately.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

